# The image's build context: what `docker build .` (and `make image`) sends to the builder. The build
# stage runs `COPY . .` and `go build ./cmd/batondeck-kanban`, which needs the Go sources and what they
# embed (web/dist above all, migrations/, the OAuth templates); nothing below is any of those.
#
# Never sent: secrets compose reads (.env holds BATONDECK_MASTER_KEY and the Postgres password) and
# local state, at any depth (a pattern without **/ matches at the context root only).
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/master.key
**/*.env
**/batondeck.sql
**/batondeck-*.tgz
/data/
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
# Build outputs and installed packages: the release binaries, the local binary, the SPA's
# node_modules (web/dist, the built SPA, is committed and embedded, so it stays), make bench's runs.
/dist/
/batondeck-kanban
/web/node_modules/
/bench/out/
/bench/results.json
# The repository's history: the image's Go has no git, so the binary is not VCS-stamped either way.
.git
**/.DS_Store
